# QuantForg Trading Core Freeze (Production Lockdown)

The LIVE trading engine is **COMPLETE and LOCKED**.

## Frozen modules (production-critical)

Do **not** modify without **explicit product-owner approval** naming the module and reason:

- Scheduler / ITE runtime (`institutional_ite_runtime.py`)
- AI Decision / confluence / pipeline
- AI Scalping
- Institutional Alpha
- Portfolio Engine
- Risk Engine
- OMS / execution bridge
- MT5 Gateway / adapter / `gateway_client`
- Position Management Engine (PME)
- Position Recovery / MT5 position truth
- Multi-symbol scanner
- Runtime state / control plane execution gates

## Forbidden without explicit approval

- New trading features, strategies, or thresholds “improvements”
- Redesign / refactor of frozen modules
- Temporary bypasses (`FORCE_FIRST_TRADE`, `ALLOW_RISK_LOCK_OVERRIDE`, validation-mode shortcuts)
- Weakening risk, margin, invalid stop/volume, market-closed, or emergency-stop guards
- Changing order_send / PME lifecycle / recovery semantics

## Allowed without freeze override

- Verified production bugs that block LIVE continuity (with regression test)
- Docs / CI / regression suite only
- Non-trading surfaces (marketing UI under Design Freeze rules)

## Gate

Before any PR touching frozen paths: regression suite `pytest -m trading_core` must pass; cite approval in the PR description.
